# Q2. HOG + SVM

### Q2(a) HOG feature length - calculation by hand (my cell size = 8 x 8)
- Image = 128 x 128, cell = 8 x 8 -> cells per side = 128 / 8 = **16**, so 16 x 16 = 256 cells.
- Block = 2 x 2 cells, stride = 1 cell -> blocks per side = 16 - 2 + 1 = **15**, so 15 x 15 = **225 blocks**.
- Each block has 2 x 2 = 4 cells, each cell has 9 orientation bins -> 4 x 9 = **36 values per block**.
- Feature length = 225 x 36 = **8100**.

(If the cell size were 16 x 16: 8 cells/side, 7 blocks/side, 49 blocks, 49 x 36 = 1764. Not used here.)

```python
def hog_feat(img, vis=False):
    return hog(img, orientations=9, pixels_per_cell=(HOG_CELL, HOG_CELL),
               cells_per_block=(2, 2), block_norm="L2-Hys", visualize=vis, feature_vector=True)

def hog_batch(X):
    return np.array([hog_feat(im) for im in X])

Htr, Hva = hog_batch(Xtr), hog_batch(Xva)

cells_side  = 128 // HOG_CELL
blocks_side = cells_side - 2 + 1
expected    = blocks_side**2 * 2 * 2 * 9
print("HOG feature length (code):", Htr.shape[1])
print("By-hand formula:", f"{blocks_side}x{blocks_side} blocks x 4 cells x 9 bins =", expected)
assert Htr.shape[1] == expected
```

