# Q4. Robustness

### Q4(a) Prediction
- **Rotation:** I think **HOG** will lose more accuracy. Reason: HOG histograms are tied to gradient directions inside fixed cells, so rotating the image changes both which orientation bins fill up and which cell contains which structure; the SIFT grid descriptor uses larger 32 x 32 patches with smoothing, so it changes less.
- **Noise:** I think **HOG** will lose more accuracy. Reason: HOG is computed from raw pixel gradients over small 8 x 8 cells, and noise adds many random strong gradients; SIFT blurs the patch (Gaussian weighting) before measuring gradients, so it averages noise out.

